* [[George Forsyth (footballer)|George Forsyth]] is a former [[association football|football]] player who played as goalkeeper throughout his sports career. The son of diplomat [[Harold Forsyth]], he entered politics as councilman of [[La Victoria District, Lima|La Victoria District]] in 2010, and as the district's mayor from 2019 until his resignation in October 2020 to run for the presidency.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.lavanguardia.com/deportes/20181008/452224045636/el-exportero-de-alianza-george-forsyth-gana-alcaldia-de-la-victoria-en-lima.html|title=El exportero de Alianza George Forsyth gana alcaldía de La Victoria, en Lima|date=8 October 2018|website=La Vanguardia|access-date=13 February 2021|archive-date=28 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210128094918/https://www.lavanguardia.com/deportes/20181008/452224045636/el-exportero-de-alianza-george-forsyth-gana-alcaldia-de-la-victoria-en-lima.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=George Forsyth renuncia a la Alcaldía de La Victoria de cara a las elecciones de 2021|url=https://rpp.pe/politica/elecciones/george-forsyth-renuncia-a-la-alcaldia-de-la-victoria-de-cara-a-noticia-1297949|website=RPP Noticias|date=12 October 2020|access-date=13 February 2021|archive-date=10 November 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201110024027/https://rpp.pe/politica/elecciones/george-forsyth-renuncia-a-la-alcaldia-de-la-victoria-de-cara-a-noticia-1297949|url-status=live}}</ref> Previously not-affiliated to party politics, he reached an agreement with [[National Restoration (Peru)|National Restoration]] for his presidential run. Upon his registration, the party filed a name-change to be reorganized into [[National Victory]] for the general election.<ref>{{Cite web|date=23 September 2020|title=Restauración Nacional confirmó inscripción de George Forsyth al partido, que ahora se llamará Victoria Nacional|url=https://rpp.pe/politica/elecciones/george-forsyth-restauracion-nacional-confirmo-inscripcion-del-alcalde-al-partido-que-ahora-se-llamara-victoria-nacional-noticia-1294257|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201210174841/https://rpp.pe/politica/elecciones/george-forsyth-restauracion-nacional-confirmo-inscripcion-del-alcalde-al-partido-que-ahora-se-llamara-victoria-nacional-noticia-1294257|archive-date=10 December 2020|access-date=13 February 2021|website=El Comercio|location=Peru}}</ref> During his campaign, he was accused of having offered a position to one of his friends in La Victoria District with an excessive remunerations; the Public Ministry opened an investigation of the situation.<ref>{{Cite web|date=2021-02-01|title=George Forsyth: Fiscalía inicia investigación preliminar en su contra por contratos a su amigo Renzo Navarro en La Victoria|url=https://elcomercio.pe/politica/justicia/george-forsyth-fiscalia-inicia-investigacion-preliminar-en-su-contra-por-contratos-a-su-amigo-renzo-navarro-en-la-victoria-noticia/|url-status=live|access-date=2021-07-20|website=[[El Comercio (Peru)]]|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210131163155/https://elcomercio.pe/politica/justicia/george-forsyth-fiscalia-inicia-investigacion-preliminar-en-su-contra-por-contratos-a-su-amigo-renzo-navarro-en-la-victoria-noticia/ |archive-date=31 January 2021 }}</ref>
* [[Ollanta Humala]] is the leader of the [[Peruvian Nationalist Party]] and the only former [[President of Peru]] running for a second non-consecutive term. A former army lieutenant colonel, he remained unpopular throughout his presidency due to the few advances his government made, despite its economic stability, in addition to serving a short pre-trial detention from 2017 to 2018 for allegedly receiving bribes from [[Odebrecht]], for which he continues to be under investigation alongside his wife, [[Nadine Heredia]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://rpp.pe/lima/actualidad/bayly-humala-encabeza-gobierno-mediocre-y-maduro-tiene-los-dias-contados-noticia-649895|title=Bayly: Humala encabeza Gobierno mediocre y Maduro tiene los días contados|website=rpp.pe|date=23 November 2013|access-date=17 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210122055120/https://rpp.pe/lima/actualidad/bayly-humala-encabeza-gobierno-mediocre-y-maduro-tiene-los-dias-contados-noticia-649895|archive-date=22 January 2021|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://revistaideele.com/ideele/content/lo-bueno-lo-malo-y-lo-feo-de-humala-2|title=Lo bueno, lo malo y lo feo de Humala + 2|website=revistaideele.com|date=8 April 2016 |access-date=17 January 2021|archive-date=19 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210119022811/https://www.revistaideele.com/ideele/content/lo-bueno-lo-malo-y-lo-feo-de-humala-2|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[Alberto Beingolea]] is the leader of the centre-right [[Christian People's Party (Peru)|Christian People's Party]].<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://elcomercio.pe/politica/elecciones/elecciones-2020-alberto-beingolea-anuncia-su-precandidatura-en-el-ppc-noticia/|title=Elecciones 2020: Alberto Beingolea anuncia su precandidatura en el PPC|date=23 October 2020|website=El Comercio|location=Peru|access-date=13 February 2021|archive-date=11 April 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210411210555/https://elcomercio.pe/politica/elecciones/elecciones-2020-alberto-beingolea-anuncia-su-precandidatura-en-el-ppc-noticia/|url-status=live |last1=Mejía Huaraca |first1=Mario }}</ref> He previously served in the [[Peruvian Congress]] from 2011 to 2016.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://andina.pe/agencia/noticia-alberto-beingolea-anuncia-no-ira-a-reeleccion-el-congreso-590767.aspx|title=Alberto Beingolea anuncia que no irá a la reelección en el Congreso|date=22 December 2015|website=andina.pe|access-date=13 February 2021|archive-date=31 March 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210331220615/https://andina.pe/agencia/noticia-alberto-beingolea-anuncia-no-ira-a-reeleccion-el-congreso-590767.aspx|url-status=live}}</ref> Prior to entering politics, he had a successful career as a sports journalist. Most recently, he ran for [[mayor of Lima]] in the [[2018 Peruvian regional and municipal elections|2018 municipal election]], in which he placed fourth.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.onpe.gob.pe/sala-prensa/notas-prensa/onpe-publica-resultados-lima-al-100/|title=ONPE Resultados al 100%|work=ONPE|date=2 November 2018|access-date=13 February 2021|archive-date=11 April 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210411210556/https://www.onpe.gob.pe/sala-prensa/notas-prensa/onpe-publica-resultados-lima-al-100/|url-status=dead}}</ref>
* [[Marco Arana]] is the leader of the [[Broad Front (Peru)|Broad Front]], a left-wing informal coalition of parties and unions.<ref>{{cite web|author=Walter Gonzalo Arcasi Mariño|date=28 September 2020|title=Elecciones 2021: pugnas en el Frente Amplio por precandidatura de Marco Arana|url=https://gestion.pe/peru/politica/frente-amplio-marco-arana-elecciones-2021-pugnas-en-el-frente-amplio-por-precandidatura-de-marco-arana-noticia/|access-date=13 February 2020|website=gestion.pe|archive-date=30 September 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200930182909/https://gestion.pe/peru/politica/frente-amplio-marco-arana-elecciones-2021-pugnas-en-el-frente-amplio-por-precandidatura-de-marco-arana-noticia/|url-status=live}}</ref> A former bishop from [[Cajamarca]], he ran unsuccessfully for the vice presidency in 2016 with [[Verónika Mendoza]] as the party's presidential nominee.<ref>{{cite web|date=27 January 2021|title=Elecciones 2021: conoce el perfil de Marco Arana, candidato del Frente Amplio|url=https://andina.pe/agencia/noticia-elecciones-2021-conoce-perfil-marco-arana-candidato-por-frente-amplio-831384.aspx|access-date=27 January 2021|website=andina.pe|archive-date=11 February 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210211074130/https://andina.pe/agencia/noticia-elecciones-2021-conoce-perfil-marco-arana-candidato-por-frente-amplio-831384.aspx|url-status=live}}</ref> He served in the [[Peruvian Congress]] from 2016 to 2019.{{Citation needed|date=July 2021}}
* [[Rafael Santos (politician)|Rafael Santos]] is [[Peru Secure Homeland]]'s nominee.<ref>{{cite web|date=27 January 2021|title=Elecciones 2021: conoce el perfil de Rafael Santos, candidato del Perú Patria Segura|url=https://andina.pe/agencia/noticia-elecciones-2021-conoce-perfil-rafael-santos-candidato-peru-patria-segura-831220.aspx|access-date=27 January 2021|website=andina.pe|archive-date=26 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210126074230/https://andina.pe/agencia/noticia-elecciones-2021-conoce-perfil-rafael-santos-candidato-peru-patria-segura-831220.aspx|url-status=live}}</ref> A businessman in the agrarian exportation area, he entered politics when he successfully ran for mayor of [[Pueblo Libre District|Pueblo Libre]] in 2006. He was reelected in 2010, but failed to attain a third term in 2014. He was previously a member of the [[Christian People's Party (Peru)|Christian People's Party]].<ref>{{cite web|date=23 December 2020|title=Elecciones 2021: conoce el perfil de Rafael Santos, candidato del Perú Patria Segura|url=https://rpp.pe/politica/elecciones/elecciones-2021-rafael-santos-el-exalcalde-que-quiere-convertirse-en-presidente-perfil-noticia-1308705|access-date=13 January 2021|website=rpp.pe|archive-date=23 December 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201223182230/https://rpp.pe/politica/elecciones/elecciones-2021-rafael-santos-el-exalcalde-que-quiere-convertirse-en-presidente-perfil-noticia-1308705|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[José Vega (politician)|José Vega]] is the leader of [[Union for Peru]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://rpp.pe/politica/elecciones/elecciones-2021-jose-vega-el-promotor-de-la-vacancia-presidencial-que-quiere-llegar-a-palacio-de-gobierno-perfil-el-poder-en-tus-manos-noticia-1308715|title=Elecciones 2021: José Vega, el promotor de la vacancia presidencial que quiere llegar a Palacio de Gobierno [Perfil]|website=rpp.pe|access-date=13 February 2020|archive-date=23 December 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201223182252/https://rpp.pe/politica/elecciones/elecciones-2021-jose-vega-el-promotor-de-la-vacancia-presidencial-que-quiere-llegar-a-palacio-de-gobierno-perfil-el-poder-en-tus-manos-noticia-1308715|url-status=live}}</ref> A congressman for the constituency of [[Lima]], he further radicalized his party following his accord with the imprisoned [[Andahuaylazo|military revolt]] leader, [[Antauro Humala]], the brother of former president [[Ollanta Humala]].<ref>{{cite web|date=10 October 2020|title=José Vega de Unión por el Perú: "Liberación de Antauro Humala está en curso"|url=https://peru21.pe/politica/jose-vega-de-union-por-el-peru-liberacion-de-antauro-humala-esta-en-curso-manuel-merino-noticia/|access-date=13 February 2021|website=peru21.pe|archive-date=21 December 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201221220341/https://peru21.pe/politica/jose-vega-de-union-por-el-peru-liberacion-de-antauro-humala-esta-en-curso-manuel-merino-noticia/|url-status=live}}</ref> He previously served a full term in the [[Peruvian Congress]] from 2006 to 2011.{{Citation needed|date=July 2021}}
* [[Ciro Gálvez]] is the leader of the [[National United Renaissance]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://andina.pe/agencia/noticia-ciro-galvez-solicita-inscripcion-su-candidatura-renacimiento-unido-nacional-827262.aspx|title=Ciro Gálvez solicita inscripción de su candidatura por Renacimiento Unido Nacional|website=andina.pe|date=22 December 2020 |access-date=7 February 2021|archive-date=23 December 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201223044441/https://andina.pe/agencia/noticia-ciro-galvez-solicita-inscripcion-su-candidatura-renacimiento-unido-nacional-827262.aspx|url-status=live}}</ref> A lawyer and notary based in [[Junín, Peru|Junín]], his platform remains conservative, declaring to be in opposition to [[LGBT]] rights. For the election, his ticket includes former pastor and businessman [[Claudio Zolla]] as his first running-mate, due to a political accord with the [[New Peru Liberal Party]], a [[libertarian]] movement led by Zolla.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://exitosanoticias.pe/v1/galvez-y-zolla-nueva-alianza-para-las-elecciones/|title=Gálvez y Zolla, nueva alianza para las elecciones|website=exitosanoticias.pe|date=October 2020|access-date=7 February 2021|archive-date=10 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210610101037/https://exitosanoticias.pe/v1/galvez-y-zolla-nueva-alianza-para-las-elecciones/|url-status=live}}</ref>
*{{ill|Andrés Alcántara (politician)|es|Andrés Alcántara (político)|lt=Andrés Alcántara}} is the leader of [[Direct Democracy (Peru)|Direct Democracy]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://rpp.pe/politica/elecciones/elecciones-2021-andres-alcantara-busca-ganar-su-primera-eleccion-para-reformar-la-constitucion-perfil-noticia-1308409|title=Elecciones 2021: Andrés Alcántara busca ganar su primera elección para reformar la Constitución [Perfil]|date=23 December 2020|access-date=13 February 2021|archive-date=23 December 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201223150740/https://rpp.pe/politica/elecciones/elecciones-2021-andres-alcantara-busca-ganar-su-primera-eleccion-para-reformar-la-constitucion-perfil-noticia-1308409|url-status=live}}</ref> A left-wing populist, he presides the FONAVI housing pensioners association, for which he campaigned strongly since early 2000s until 2010 for the government's full pension devolution, which was achieved following via [[2010 Peruvian FONAVI funds referendum|referendum]]. His campaign platform is poised in reforming and eventually replacing the [[Constitution of Peru]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://canaln.pe/actualidad/andres-alcantara-candidato-presidencial-democracia-directa-apuesta-nueva-constitucion-n431238|title=Andrés Alcántara: Candidato de Democracia Directa apuesta por una nueva Constitución|access-date=13 February 2021|date=11 February 2021|archive-date=11 February 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210211204930/https://canaln.pe/actualidad/andres-alcantara-candidato-presidencial-democracia-directa-apuesta-nueva-constitucion-n431238|url-status=live}}</ref> He ran for the vice presidency in the last three general elections.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://andina.pe/agencia/noticia-elecciones-2021-conoce-perfil-andres-alcantara-candidato-democracia-directa-831378.aspx|title=Elecciones 2021: conoce el perfil de Andrés Alcántara, candidato por Democracia Directa|author=Carlos Lezama|access-date=13 February 2021|date=27 January 2021|archive-date=11 February 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210211083208/https://andina.pe/agencia/noticia-elecciones-2021-conoce-perfil-andres-alcantara-candidato-democracia-directa-831378.aspx|url-status=live}}</ref>

