== Aftermath ==
=== Overturn attempts ===
After the publication of the quick count and the first official results, protests by supporters of both Free Peru and Popular Force took place.<ref>{{cite web |date=2021-06-08 |title=Simpatizantes de Castillo y Fujimori protestan en exteriores de la ONPE |url=https://larepublica.pe/elecciones/2021/06/08/elecciones-2021-simpatizantes-de-castillo-y-fujimori-protestan-en-exteriores-de-la-onpe-pltc/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210609022313/https://larepublica.pe/elecciones/2021/06/08/elecciones-2021-simpatizantes-de-castillo-y-fujimori-protestan-en-exteriores-de-la-onpe-pltc/ |archive-date=9 June 2021 |access-date=2021-06-24 |website=[[La República (Peru)|La República]] |language=es}}</ref> Amid the fraud accusations and the final vote count, there were nearly daily protests and marches, mostly in the capital [[Lima]].<ref>{{cite web |date=2021-06-24 |title=Peru political fog thickens as election count official quits |url=https://www.swissinfo.ch/eng/peru-political-fog-thickens-as-election-count-official-quits/46734070 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210624220559/https://www.swissinfo.ch/eng/peru-political-fog-thickens-as-election-count-official-quits/46734070 |archive-date=24 June 2021 |access-date=2021-06-24 |website=Swissinfo}}</ref> Besides Fujimori supporters, groups opposed to Castillo, mobilized by the fear of communism or aversion to the left wing, mobilized asking for the annulment of the elections.<ref name=":38">{{cite web |date=2021-06-19 |title=El Perú que las elecciones nos dejó ver |url=https://www.elespectador.com/mundo/america/el-peru-que-las-elecciones-nos-dejo-ver/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210620043417/https://www.elespectador.com/mundo/america/el-peru-que-las-elecciones-nos-dejo-ver/ |archive-date=20 June 2021 |access-date=2021-06-24 |website=El Espectador |language=es}}</ref> After exit polls gave the victory to Keiko Fujimori over Pedro Castillo, supporters of Free Peru mobilized to the offices of the ONPE to protest against a possible fraud against their candidate,<ref>{{cite web |last=Acosta |first=Sebastián |date=2021-06-06 |title=Segunda vuelta {{!}} Decenas de manifestantes protestan cerca a sede de la ONPE tras resultados a boca de urna |url=https://rpp.pe/politica/elecciones/segunda-vuelta-decenas-de-manifestantes-protestan-cerca-a-sede-de-la-onpe-por-resultados-a-boca-de-urna-noticia-1340837 |access-date=2021-07-10 |website=RPP |language=es}}</ref> bringing banners saying "no to the fraud."<ref>{{cite web |date=2021-06-07 |title=Elecciones 2021: simpatizantes de Perú Libre realizan plantón frente a la ONPE |url=https://gestion.pe/peru/elecciones-2021-simpatizantes-de-peru-libre-realizan-planton-frente-a-la-onpe-nndc-noticia/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210607201744/https://gestion.pe/peru/elecciones-2021-simpatizantes-de-peru-libre-realizan-planton-frente-a-la-onpe-nndc-noticia/ |archive-date=7 June 2021 |access-date=2021-07-10 |website=Gestión |language=es}}</ref> From [[Tacabamba District|Tacabamba]], [[Cajamarca]],<ref>{{cite web |date=2021-06-07 |title=Simpatizantes de Perú Libre gritan "¡no al fraude!" y Pedro Castillo pide salir en paz a las calles |url=https://www.expreso.com.pe/elecciones-2021/simpatizantes-de-peru-libre-gritan-no-al-fraude-y-pedro-castillo-pide-salir-en-paz-a-las-calles/ |access-date=2021-07-10 |website=Diario Expreso}}</ref> Castillo called upon his followers and supporters on Twitter to "defend the votes" and go to the streets to "defend democracy."<ref>{{cite web |date=2021-06-07 |title=Elecciones 2021: Pedro Castillo pide a personeros "estar atentos a defender cada voto" |url=https://gestion.pe/peru/politica/elecciones-2021-pedro-castillo-pide-a-personeros-estar-atentos-a-defender-cada-voto-keiko-fujimori-segunda-vuelta-nndc-noticia/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210607011811/https://gestion.pe/peru/politica/elecciones-2021-pedro-castillo-pide-a-personeros-estar-atentos-a-defender-cada-voto-keiko-fujimori-segunda-vuelta-nndc-noticia/ |archive-date=7 June 2021 |access-date=2021-07-10 |website=Gestión |language=es}}</ref> Protests against Fujimori and an alleged fraud took place in cities such as [[Juliaca]], [[Puno]], and [[Ilave]].<ref>{{cite web |date=2021-06-06 |title=Partidarios de Perú Libre de Juliaca, Puno e Ilave protestan por supuesto fraude electoral |url=https://larepublica.pe/sociedad/2021/06/06/partidarios-de-peru-libre-de-juliaca-puno-e-ilave-protestan-por-supuesto-fraude-electoral-lrsd/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210607044421/https://larepublica.pe/sociedad/2021/06/06/partidarios-de-peru-libre-de-juliaca-puno-e-ilave-protestan-por-supuesto-fraude-electoral-lrsd/ |archive-date=7 June 2021 |access-date=2021-07-10 |website=[[La República (Peru)|La República]] |language=es-PE}}</ref> During a mobilization in the San Martín Square in Lima, [[Ronda Campesina|''rondas campesinas'']] supportive of Castillo carried [[machete]]s with them.<ref>{{cite web |date=2021-06-18 |title=Ronderos en Lima: uso de machetes en movilización genera polémica |url=https://caretas.pe/nacional/ronderos-en-lima-uso-de-machetes-en-movilizacion-genera-polemica/ |access-date=2021-06-24 |website=caretas.pe |language=es |archive-date=3 July 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210703054122/https://caretas.pe/nacional/ronderos-en-lima-uso-de-machetes-en-movilizacion-genera-polemica/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> On 14 July, several pro-Fujimori protesters gathered at the Government Palace demanding an audit of the election. Protesters clashed with the [[National Police of Peru]], and [[Ministry of Health (Peru)|Health Minister]] [[Óscar Ugarte]] and [[Ministry of Housing, Construction and Sanitation (Peru)|Housing Minister]] Solangel Fernández were attacked during the protests.<ref>{{Cite web |date=14 July 2021 |title=Fuerza Popular: Simpatizantes fujimoristas se enfrentaron a la Policía para llegar a Palacio de Gobierno |url=https://rpp.pe/lima/actualidad/fuerza-popular-simpatizantes-fujimoristas-se-enfrentaron-a-la-policia-para-llegar-a-palacio-de-gobierno-noticia-1347486 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210715033223/https://rpp.pe/lima/actualidad/fuerza-popular-simpatizantes-fujimoristas-se-enfrentaron-a-la-policia-para-llegar-a-palacio-de-gobierno-noticia-1347486 |archive-date=15 July 2021 |access-date=15 July 2021}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=15 July 2021 |title=Seguidores de Keiko Fujimori marchan a Palacio y atacan el coche de dos ministros con ellos dentro |url=https://www.elmundo.es/internacional/2021/07/15/60efa2aefdddffd0aa8b45db.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210715032346/https://www.elmundo.es/internacional/2021/07/15/60efa2aefdddffd0aa8b45db.html |archive-date=15 July 2021 |access-date=15 July 2021}}</ref> On 15 July, Sagasti reaffirmed that there was no evidence of voter fraud.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Peru's President: 2021 elections were clean, there was no fraud |date=15 July 2021 |url=https://andina.pe/Ingles/noticia-perus-president-2021-elections-were-clean-there-was-no-fraud-853417.aspx |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210715223426/https://andina.pe/Ingles/noticia-perus-president-2021-elections-were-clean-there-was-no-fraud-853417.aspx |archive-date=15 July 2021 |access-date=15 July 2021}}</ref>

Following reports of Castillo's apparent victory, Fujimori and her supporters made unsubstantiated claims of [[electoral fraud]], leading efforts to overturn the election with support of citizens in Lima.{{sfn|Asensio|Camacho|González|Grompone|2021|pp=69-71}}<ref name=":37" /><ref name=":31" /><ref name=":272" /><ref name=":35">{{cite news|title=With election fraud claims, Peru's Keiko Fujimori takes a page from the Trump playbook. She's not alone.|author=Anthony Faiola, Claire Parker and Terrence McCoy|newspaper=The Washington Post|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2021/06/16/trump-playbook-peru-democracy/|access-date=22 June 2021|issn=0190-8286|archive-date=21 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210621072244/https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2021/06/16/trump-playbook-peru-democracy/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=":29">{{cite news|last=Applebaum|first=Anne|date=17 June 2021|title=Democracy Is Surprisingly Easy to Undermine|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2021/06/trump-fraud-stop-steal-copycats/619226/|access-date=22 June 2021|work=The Atlantic|archive-date=20 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210620121009/https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2021/06/trump-fraud-stop-steal-copycats/619226/|url-status=live}}</ref> Rumors spread of a possible [[coup d'état]] against Castillo, if he were declared the official winner of the presidential election.<ref name=":31" /> A letter signed by almost one-hundred retired officers of the Peruvian armed forces was written calling on current military leaders in Peru to refuse recognizing the election of Castillo into the presidency.<ref name=":31" /> President Sagasti condemned the letter, stating: "They want to incite top commanders of the Army, Navy, and Air force to break the rule of law."<ref name=":31" /><ref name=":37" />{{sfn|Asensio|Camacho|González|Grompone|2021|pp=27–71}} According to analysts, Peru was more susceptible to unrest as a result of Fujimori's narrative since democratic institutions are weaker in the nation.<ref name=":37" /> Minor clashes occurred in Lima between Fujimori supporters from the capital city and Castillo supporters from other regions, with [[rondas campesinas]] equipped with sticks and machetes arriving in the [[Historic Centre of Lima]] to defend Castillo's election and dissuade Fujimori protesters.{{sfn|Asensio|Camacho|González|Grompone|2021|pp=69-71}}

Senior fellow of the [[Washington Office on Latin America]] Jo Marie Burt described the overturn attempts as "a slow-motion conspiracy to prevent Castillo from becoming president", with ''[[The Guardian]]'' reporting that if Castillo was prevented from becoming president by 28 July 2021, a new election would be initiated.<ref name=":4" /> Fujimori's statements about possibly overturning the election, along with her use of [[fake news]] and legal challenges, were also described as being inspired by the [[attempts to overturn the 2020 U.S. presidential election]] by former U.S. president [[Donald Trump]].{{sfn|Asensio|Camacho|González|Grompone|2021|p=91}}<ref name=":37" /><ref name=":31" /><ref name=":35" /><ref name=":29" /> According to [[Cornell University]] professor of Latin American politics Kenneth Roberts, "[w]hen the credibility is called into question the way it has been by Trump and the Republicans in the U.S., it creates a bad example that other leaders and countries can follow, providing a template to change results they don't like."<ref name=":35" />

On 18 June, former Supreme Court President Javier Villa Stein filed a complaint for protection by describing the ballot vote as "questioned", arguing an alleged "electoral process flawed by various acts that undermine the popular will" and asking the judiciary branch to "declare the election void."<ref>{{cite web|date=18 June 2021|title=Presentan recurso al PJ para declarar nula elección de segunda vuelta|url=https://larepublica.pe/elecciones/2021/06/18/elecciones-2021-presentan-recurso-al-poder-judicial-para-declarar-nula-eleccion-de-segunda-vuelta-pltc/|url-status=live|access-date=24 June 2021|website=[[La República (Peru)|La República]]|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210619031349/https://larepublica.pe/elecciones/2021/06/18/elecciones-2021-presentan-recurso-al-poder-judicial-para-declarar-nula-eleccion-de-segunda-vuelta-pltc/ |archive-date=19 June 2021 }}</ref> Lawyer Renán Galindo Peralta requested that it be rejected outright considering it inadmissible because it did not fall under the Organic Law of Elections and because the judicial branch lacked the powers to annul elections.<ref>{{cite web|date=21 June 2021|title=Piden rechazar demanda de Javier Villa Stein para anular la segunda vuelta|url=https://larepublica.pe/elecciones/2021/06/21/elecciones-2021-piden-rechazar-demanda-de-javier-villa-stein-para-anular-la-segunda-vuelta-pltc/?ref=lre|url-status=live|access-date=24 June 2021|website=[[La República (Peru)|La República]]|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210624231127/https://larepublica.pe/elecciones/2021/06/21/elecciones-2021-piden-rechazar-demanda-de-javier-villa-stein-para-anular-la-segunda-vuelta-pltc/?ref=lre |archive-date=24 June 2021 }}</ref>

==== Claims of fraud ====
To avoid the questions of election legitimacy, election authorities in Peru approved the use of [[election monitoring]].<ref name=":27">{{cite web |date=4 June 2021 |title=¿Cuántos observadores internacionales vigilarán la segunda vuelta electoral? |url=https://ojo-publico.com/2779/cuantos-observadores-internacionales-vigilaran-las-elecciones |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210608161217/https://ojo-publico.com/2779/cuantos-observadores-internacionales-vigilaran-las-elecciones |archive-date=8 June 2021 |access-date=8 June 2021 |website=[[Ojo Público]] |language=es}}</ref> In total, one hundred and fifty observers (ninety-nine in Peru and fifty-one abroad) were approved to observe elections throughout Peru.<ref name=":27" /> The origin of the observers were from twenty-two different countries, with thirty-five observers from the [[Organization of American States]], while others were from Argentina, Colombia, Costa Rica, Ecuador, El Salvador, Guatemala, Mexico, Panama, Paraguay, Spain, Switzerland, the United States, and Uruguay.<ref name=":27" /> Observer approval required providing election authorities observation plans; these plans included protocols to inform authorities of crimes, violations of electoral law or any complaints they collected.<ref name=":27" /> Observers were then responsible with providing an official, final report to authorities.<ref name=":27" /> According to [[OjoPúblico]], "the observers carry out the review of the activities of election day, ranging from the installation of the voting tables, the conditioning of the secret chambers, the conformity of the ballots, the minutes, the amphorae and any other electoral material, to the counting, the counting of the vote and the transfer of the electoral records at the end of the day."<ref name=":27" />

After Castillo took the lead during the ballot-counting process, Fujimori promoted false claims of electoral fraud.{{sfn|Asensio|Camacho|González|Grompone|2021|p=91}}<ref name=":272">{{cite web|last1=Collyns|first1=Dan|date=8 June 2021|title=Peru elections: Fujimori's fraud claims criticised as rival's narrow lead widens|url=http://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jun/08/keiko-fujimori-claims-irregularities-peru-presidential-election-pedro-castillo|access-date=8 June 2021|website=The Guardian|archive-date=8 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210608042309/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jun/08/keiko-fujimori-claims-irregularities-peru-presidential-election-pedro-castillo|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=":37"/><ref name=":282">{{cite web|date=8 June 2021|title=Keiko Fujimori alleges fraud in tight Peru election|url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20210608-keiko-fujimori-alleges-fraud-in-tight-peru-election|access-date=8 June 2021|publisher=France 24|archive-date=8 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210608042756/https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20210608-keiko-fujimori-alleges-fraud-in-tight-peru-election|url-status=live}}</ref> In a media event following election day, Fujimori alleged that a "series of irregularities" had occurred, presenting photographs and videos in an attempt to support her allegations, while also accusing Free Peru of attempting to "distort and delay" the election process.<ref name=":272"/><ref name=":282"/> Fujimori argued that it consisted in the challenge of polling stations where Fujimori would register a greater number of votes than his opponent, previous training talks by Free Peru in which they ask their representatives to arrive early at the polling stations to ensure control of the polling stations where titular members did not attend and irregularities in the vote count.<ref>{{cite web|date=8 June 2021|title=Keiko Fujimori denuncia "fraude sistemático" en comicios|url=https://www.dw.com/es/keiko-fujimori-denuncia-fraude-sistem%C3%A1tico-en-comicios/a-57809388|url-status=live|access-date=15 June 2021|website=[[Deutsche Welle]]|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210608033104/https://www.dw.com/es/keiko-fujimori-denuncia-fraude-sistem%C3%A1tico-en-comicios/a-57809388 |archive-date=8 June 2021 }}</ref> To support the complaints, Keiko's running mate, [[Luis Galarreta]], assured that Free Peru did a "high number of challenges" to electoral acts in which Keiko was favoured so they could not be counted to the final estimate until they were evaluated first by the National Jury of Elections.<ref>{{cite web|date=7 June 2021|title=Luis Galarreta: En el 80% de las actas impugnadas tenemos una ventaja|url=https://gestion.pe/peru/politica/luis-galarreta-en-el-80-de-las-actas-impugnadas-tenemos-una-ventaja-nndc-noticia/|url-status=live|access-date=15 June 2021|website=Gestión|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210608045217/https://gestion.pe/peru/politica/luis-galarreta-en-el-80-de-las-actas-impugnadas-tenemos-una-ventaja-nndc-noticia/ |archive-date=8 June 2021 }}</ref> According to the complaint, over 1 300 voting acts were challenged by Free Peru;<ref name=":37">{{cite web|date=8 June 2021|title=Claves del supuesto "fraude sistemático" denunciado por Keiko Fujimori|url=https://www.swissinfo.ch/spa/per%C3%BA-elecciones_claves-del-supuesto--fraude-sistem%C3%A1tico--denunciado-por-keiko-fujimori/46688860|access-date=24 June 2021|website=Swissinfo|language=es}}</ref> however, the first claims were rebutted by national electoral entities.<ref>{{cite web|date=8 June 2021|title=Claves del supuesto 'fraude sistemático' denunciado por Keiko Fujimori|url=https://www.swissinfo.ch/spa/per%C3%BA-elecciones_claves-del-supuesto--fraude-sistem%C3%A1tico--denunciado-por-keiko-fujimori/46688860|url-status=live|access-date=20 July 2021|website=Swissinfo|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210609191657/https://www.swissinfo.ch/spa/per%C3%BA-elecciones_claves-del-supuesto--fraude-sistem%C3%A1tico--denunciado-por-keiko-fujimori/46688860 |archive-date=9 June 2021 }}</ref> After the resolution of the challenged votes and the acts observed by the Special Electoral Juries, the National Office of Electoral Processes published the total results on 15 June, in which Pedro Castillo surpassed Keiko Fujimori in number of votes.<ref>{{cite web|date=23 June 2021|title=Resultados ONPE 100% actas contabilizadas: Pedro Castillo 50.125% y Keiko Fujimori 49.875%|url=https://elcomercio.pe/politica/elecciones/resultados-onpe-100-elecciones-2021-pedro-castillo-50125-y-keiko-fujimori-49875-de-actas-contabilizadas-cifras-oficiales-de-segunda-vuelta-de-elecciones-generales-peru-2021-conteo-de-votos-peru-libre-fuerza-popular-oficina-nacional-de-procesos-electorales-jne-nuevo-presidente-resultados-oficiales-onpe-noticia/|url-status=live|access-date=24 June 2021|website=[[El Comercio (Peru)|El Comercio]]|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210621184039/https://elcomercio.pe/politica/elecciones/resultados-onpe-100-elecciones-2021-pedro-castillo-50125-y-keiko-fujimori-49875-de-actas-contabilizadas-cifras-oficiales-de-segunda-vuelta-de-elecciones-generales-peru-2021-conteo-de-votos-peru-libre-fuerza-popular-oficina-nacional-de-procesos-electorales-jne-nuevo-presidente-resultados-oficiales-onpe-noticia/ |archive-date=21 June 2021 }}</ref>

According to ''The Guardian'', various international observers countered Fujimori's claims, stating that the election process was conducted in accordance with international standards.<ref name=":272" /> Observers from the Inter-American Union of Electoral Organizations, the [[Organization of American States]], and the [[Progressive International]] denied any instances of widespread fraud and praised the accuracy of the elections.<ref>{{Cite web|date=8 June 2021|title="We must defend popular sovereignty in Peru"|url=https://progressive.international/wire/2021-06-08-we-must-defend-popular-sovereignty-in-peru/en|access-date=10 June 2021|website=Progressive International|language=en|archive-date=10 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210610015722/https://progressive.international/wire/2021-06-08-we-must-defend-popular-sovereignty-in-peru/en/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=9 June 2021|title=Perú: Castillo se proclama vencedor sin los resultados definitivos del conteo oficial|url=https://www.france24.com/es/am%C3%A9rica-latina/20210609-peru-castillo-declara-ganador-sin-resultados-oficiales|access-date=10 June 2021|publisher=France 24|archive-date=10 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210610015717/https://www.france24.com/es/am%C3%A9rica-latina/20210609-peru-castillo-declara-ganador-sin-resultados-oficiales|url-status=live}}</ref> ''The Guardian'' also reported that analysts and political observers criticized Fujimori's remarks, noting that it made her appear desperate after losing her third presidential run in a ten-year period.<ref name=":272"/> Fernando Tuesta, political scientist from the Pontifical Catholic University of Peru, stated: "It's extremely regrettable that when the result is not favourable, that the candidate talks about fraud. It's terrible, ... They have been talking about fraud because they don't want to respect the result."<ref name=":272"/> On 9 June, Fujimori sought to have around 200,000 votes annulled and for 300,000 votes to be reviewed.<ref>{{cite web|date=10 June 2021|title=Fujimori seeks ballots annulled as leftist Castillo leads in Peru's presidential vote|url=https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20210610-fujimori-seeks-ballots-annulled-as-leftist-castillo-leads-in-peru-election|access-date=10 June 2021|publisher=France 24|archive-date=10 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210610043438/https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20210610-fujimori-seeks-ballots-annulled-as-leftist-castillo-leads-in-peru-election|url-status=live}}</ref>

On 10 June, the Peruvian Prosecution asked for the detention of Keiko on charges of violating the conditional liberty that she was granted during the open criminal process against her.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Fowks|first=Jacqueline|date=2021-06-10|title=La Fiscalía de Perú pide prisión para Keiko Fujimori por el 'caso Odebrecht' en plena pugna por las presidenciales|url=https://elpais.com/internacional/2021-06-10/la-fiscalia-peruana-pide-prision-para-keiko-fujimori-por-el-caso-odebrecht.html|url-status=live|access-date=2021-07-20|website=[[El País]]|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210610183845/https://elpais.com/internacional/2021-06-10/la-fiscalia-peruana-pide-prision-para-keiko-fujimori-por-el-caso-odebrecht.html |archive-date=10 June 2021 }}</ref> On 17 June, Fujimori repeated claims of voter fraud.<ref>{{cite web|date=17 June 2021|title=Presidential hopeful Fujimori repeats Peru vote fraud claims|url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20210617-presidential-hopeful-fujimori-repeats-peru-vote-fraud-claims|access-date=28 June 2021|website=France 24|language=en|archive-date=30 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210630044721/https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20210617-presidential-hopeful-fujimori-repeats-peru-vote-fraud-claims|url-status=live}}</ref> On 28 June, Fujimori traveled to the [[Government Palace (Peru)|Government Palace]] and personally delivered demands to President [[Francisco Sagasti]] to initiate an audit of the results by international entities.<ref name=":19" /> On 30 June, several members of the [[Popular Force]] party traveled to the [[Pan American Union Building|OAS Building]] in [[Washington, D.C.]], to publicize the voter fraud claims, with sociologist Francesca Emanuele condemning them as "coup plotters" during a press conference.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://wapa.pe/mujer/2021/06/30/sociologa-iquena-francesca-emanuele-encara-delegacion-fujimorista-en-oea-son-golpistas-actualidad-video-8514|title=Socióloga iqueña encara a delegación fujimorista en la OEA: 'Son golpistas'|website=Wapa|date=30 June 2021|accessdate=8 July 2021|archive-date=20 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210720133144/https://wapa.pe/mujer/2021/06/30/sociologa-iquena-francesca-emanuele-encara-delegacion-fujimorista-en-oea-son-golpistas-actualidad-video-8514|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Encaran a fujimoristas que viajaron a Washington: 'Ustedes son vistos como golpistas'|url=https://elpopular.pe/actualidad/2021/06/30/encaran-fujimoristas-conferencia-prensa-washington-ustedes-son-vistos-como-golpistas-video-71552|access-date=8 July 2021|website=El Popular|language=es|date=30 June 2021|archive-date=9 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210709183638/https://elpopular.pe/actualidad/2021/06/30/encaran-fujimoristas-conferencia-prensa-washington-ustedes-son-vistos-como-golpistas-video-71552|url-status=live}}</ref> On 2 July, Sagasti rejected a request to audit the second round of the election, and Fujimori accused Sagasti of abdicating his "great responsibility to ensure fair elections."<ref>{{cite news|url=https://canaln.pe/actualidad/keiko-fujimori-sagasti-abdico-su-gran-responsabilidad-garantizar-elecciones-limpias-n436764|title=Keiko Fujimori: 'Sagasti abdicó de su gran responsabilidad de garantizar elecciones limpias'|agency=Canal N|language=es|date=2 July 2021|accessdate=4 July 2021|archive-date=3 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210703184818/https://canaln.pe/actualidad/keiko-fujimori-sagasti-abdico-su-gran-responsabilidad-garantizar-elecciones-limpias-n436764|url-status=live}}</ref> On 19 July, Fujimori admitted her defeat but reaffirmed that "votes were stolen" from her.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.usnews.com/news/world/articles/2021-07-19/perus-fujimori-admits-defeat-in-presidential-election-lashes-out-at-socialist-rival |title=Peru Socialist Castillo Confirmed President After Lengthy Battle Over Results |work=U.S. News & World Report |agency=Reuters |date=19 July 2021 |access-date=2 January 2022 |url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210720004537/https://www.usnews.com/news/world/articles/2021-07-19/perus-fujimori-admits-defeat-in-presidential-election-lashes-out-at-socialist-rival |archive-date=20 July 2021 }}</ref>

=====Montesinos and JNE scandal=====
{{Further|Vladimiro Montesinos#Vladi-audios}}
On 25 June, former 2001 and 2016 presidential candidate [[Fernando Olivera (politician)|Fernando Olivera]] revealed audio tapes, alleging that [[Vladimiro Montesinos]], who was the right hand man to former President [[Alberto Fujimori]] currently serving a prison sentence for crimes committed during the Fujimori period, was behind the attempts for Keiko Fujimori to be declared as the winner of the second round against Castillo, including through the payment of bribes to electoral officials and influencing the [[National Jury of Elections]]. The [[National Penitentiary Institute (Peru)|National Penitentiary Institute]] and [[Peruvian Navy]] announced an investigation, confirming that Montesinos made two phone calls from Callao Naval Base where he is jailed, on 10 and 23 June to unauthorised persons coordinating the effort to overturn the election.<ref>{{cite web|date=25 June 2021|title=Vladimiro Montesinos: INPE and the Navy opened an investigation by telephone communications|url=https://today.in-24.com/News/30338.html|access-date=26 June 2021|website=Today in 24|archive-date=26 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210626092011/https://today.in-24.com/News/30338.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=25 June 2021|title=Marina e INPE investigan llamadas de Montesinos desde Base Naval|url=https://gestion.pe/peru/politica/vladimiro-montesinos-marina-de-guerra-e-inpe-investigan-llamadas-telefonicas-desde-base-naval-jurado-nacional-de-elecciones-fernando-olivera-jne-nndc-noticia/|access-date=26 June 2021|website=Gestión|language=es|archive-date=25 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210625225040/https://gestion.pe/peru/politica/vladimiro-montesinos-marina-de-guerra-e-inpe-investigan-llamadas-telefonicas-desde-base-naval-jurado-nacional-de-elecciones-fernando-olivera-jne-nndc-noticia/|url-status=live}}</ref>

Further reports showed that Montesinos allegedly was able to make seventeen phone calls from a [[landline]] phone to retired military officer Pedro Rejas, reportedly suggesting to Rejas that bribes needed to be paid and that Fujimori's husband, an American, go to the United States embassy in Lima to present "documentation of the fraud" to the Office of Regional Affairs and [[Central Intelligence Agency]].<ref name=":4"/><ref name=":30">{{cite web|date=1 July 2021|title=Operaciones 'irregulares' del 'Doc' desde la Base Naval|url=https://www.idl-reporteros.pe/operaciones-irregulares-del-doc-desde-la-base-naval/|access-date=2 July 2021|website=IDL Reporteros|language=es|archive-date=2 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210702030549/https://www.idl-reporteros.pe/operaciones-irregulares-del-doc-desde-la-base-naval/|url-status=live}}</ref> According to [[IDL-Reporteros]], Montesinos suggests that the documentation would reach President [[Joe Biden]] and that his administration would condemn the election as interference from Cuba, Nicaragua, and Venezuela, subsequently giving Fujimori's claims of fraud more weight.<ref name=":30"/>

=== Reactions ===

==== Domestic ====
[[Lourdes Flores]], leader of the [[Christian People's Party (Peru)|Christian People's Party]], which supported Fujimori in the election, argued carrying out her own analysis of certain electoral acts, concluding that there was a mechanism to "improperly incline the vote" in favor of Pedro Castillo.<ref>{{cite web|date=14 June 2021|title=Lourdes Flores denuncia casos de 'distorsiones a la verdad electoral' en perjuicio de Keiko Fujimori|url=https://rpp.pe/peru/actualidad/elecciones-2021-lourdes-flores-denuncia-casos-de-distorsiones-a-la-verdad-electoral-en-perjuicio-de-keiko-fujimori-noticia-1342031|url-status=live|access-date=15 June 2021|website=RPP|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210614143345/https://rpp.pe/peru/actualidad/elecciones-2021-lourdes-flores-denuncia-casos-de-distorsiones-a-la-verdad-electoral-en-perjuicio-de-keiko-fujimori-noticia-1342031 |archive-date=14 June 2021 }}</ref> [[Rafael López Aliaga]], former presidential candidate for [[Popular Renewal]] who supported Fujimori as well, argued that the second round or ballot should be repeated because "there is a fraud that cannot be covered up anymore".<ref>{{cite web|date=14 June 2021|title=Rafael López Aliaga pide que la segunda vuelta se desarrolle otra vez: "Aquí hay un fraude que ya no se puede tapar"|url=https://willax.tv/rafael-lopez-aliaga-pide-que-la-segunda-vuelta-se-desarrolle-otra-vez-aqui-hay-un-fraude-que-ya-no-se-puede-tapar/|url-status=live|access-date=15 June 2021|website=Willax|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210615035823/https://willax.tv/rafael-lopez-aliaga-pide-que-la-segunda-vuelta-se-desarrolle-otra-vez-aqui-hay-un-fraude-que-ya-no-se-puede-tapar/ |archive-date=15 June 2021 }}</ref> [[Alfredo Barnechea]], former candidate for [[Popular Action (Peru)|Popular Action]], affirmed that the irregularities detected were "massive" and that therefore the ballot should be repeated with international observation or else whoever is elected "will not have any legitimacy."<ref>{{cite web|date=15 June 2021|title=Barnechea pide nueva segunda vuelta: Hay que repetirla con observación internacional y no con esos mamarrachos de la OEA|url=https://www.expreso.com.pe/elecciones-2021/barnechea-pide-nueva-segunda-vuelta-hay-que-repetirla-con-observacion-internacional-y-no-con-esos-mamarrachos-de-la-oea/|url-status=live|access-date=15 June 2021|website=Diario Expreso|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210615152611/https://www.expreso.com.pe/elecciones-2021/barnechea-pide-nueva-segunda-vuelta-hay-que-repetirla-con-observacion-internacional-y-no-con-esos-mamarrachos-de-la-oea/ |archive-date=15 June 2021 }}</ref>

Former Peruvian prime minister [[Salvador del Solar]] declared that "there is no legal basis to denounce fraud nor to request new elections."<ref>{{cite web|date=15 June 2021|title=Salvador del Solar: 'No hay base legal para denunciar fraude ni para pedir nuevas elecciones'|url=https://lucidez.pe/salvador-del-solar-no-hay-base-legal-para-denunciar-fraude-ni-para-pedir-nuevas-elecciones/|url-status=live|access-date=15 June 2021|website=Lucidez|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210615183223/https://lucidez.pe/salvador-del-solar-no-hay-base-legal-para-denunciar-fraude-ni-para-pedir-nuevas-elecciones/ |archive-date=15 June 2021 }}</ref> The Secretary General of the Transparency Civil Association, Iván Lanegra, declared that "there is no indication of fraud" in the Peruvian elections.<ref>{{cite web|date=22 June 2021|title=El fujimorismo se topa con una pared: el tribunal electoral entra en la fase final para determinar un ganador en Perú|url=https://elpais.com/internacional/2021-06-22/el-fujimorismo-se-topa-con-una-pared-el-tribunal-electoral-entra-en-la-fase-final-para-determinar-un-ganador-en-peru.html|url-status=live|access-date=23 June 2021|website=[[El País]]|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210622211338/https://elpais.com/internacional/2021-06-22/el-fujimorismo-se-topa-con-una-pared-el-tribunal-electoral-entra-en-la-fase-final-para-determinar-un-ganador-en-peru.html |archive-date=22 June 2021 }}</ref> [[Verónika Mendoza]], former candidate who endorsed Castillo, described Popular Will's annulment requests as attempts to dismiss the electoral results and "hit democracy."<ref>{{cite news|date=24 June 2021|title=Verónika Mendoza: 'Pretenden desconocer el resultado electoral, generar caos y golpear la democracia'|url=https://elcomercio.pe/politica/elecciones/veronika-mendoza-pretenden-desconocer-el-resultado-electoral-generar-caos-y-golpear-la-democracia-elecciones-generales-del-peru-2021-peru-libre-pedro-castillo-fuerza-popular-keiko-fujimori-nndc-noticia/|url-status=live|access-date=25 June 2021|website=[[El Comercio (Peru)|El Comercio]]|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210617213815/https://elcomercio.pe/politica/elecciones/veronika-mendoza-pretenden-desconocer-el-resultado-electoral-generar-caos-y-golpear-la-democracia-elecciones-generales-del-peru-2021-peru-libre-pedro-castillo-fuerza-popular-keiko-fujimori-nndc-noticia/ |archive-date=17 June 2021 }}</ref> Journalist César Hildebrandt said that by dismissing the election results, "what Keiko Fujimori is doing is equivalent to a soft coup", describing the allegations of Fujimori's alleged fraud as "Andean Trumpism."<ref>{{cite web|date=13 June 2021|title=César Hildebrandt: 'Lo que está haciendo Keiko Fujimori equivale a un golpe de Estado blando, es trumpismo andino'|url=https://www.latercera.com/earlyaccess/noticia/cesar-hildebrandt-lo-que-esta-haciendo-keiko-fujimori-equivale-a-un-golpe-de-estado-blando-es-trumpismo-andino/I4ZTIU6ZTBE55JBTKBVYPYMQY4/|url-status=live|access-date=15 June 2021|website=La Tercera|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210614122206/https://www.latercera.com/earlyaccess/noticia/cesar-hildebrandt-lo-que-esta-haciendo-keiko-fujimori-equivale-a-un-golpe-de-estado-blando-es-trumpismo-andino/I4ZTIU6ZTBE55JBTKBVYPYMQY4/ |archive-date=14 June 2021 }}</ref>

On 23 June, Luis Arce, a judge on the [[National Jury of Elections]] (JNE), resigned and alleged bias on the jury which had rejected ten Fujimori requests to annul Castillo votes. On its Twitter account, JNE rejected Arce's allegation of bias as "offensive", and said its judges were not allowed to resign in the middle of reviews of cases, so he would be suspended instead, and a provisional replacement found "to avoid delaying our work." Castillo's Free Peru party said the resignation was aimed at "preventing the proclamation of Pedro Castillo, thereby ignoring the popular vote, breaking democracy and installing a coup d'état with silk gloves." In the wake of Arce's resignation, a lawyer representing Fujimori said that the government should consider asking the [[Organization of American States]] (OAS) to audit the electoral process, as was done during the [[2019 Bolivian political crisis]]. The OAS stated that its mission to the country had not found any issues in the conduct of the election.<ref>{{cite news|date=25 June 2021|title=Peru political fog thickens as election count official quits|work=Reuters|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/peru-political-fog-thickens-election-count-official-quits-2021-06-24/|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210625150622/https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/peru-political-fog-thickens-election-count-official-quits-2021-06-24/|archive-date=25 June 2021|accessdate=26 June 2021}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|date=24 June 2021|title=Misión de observación de la OEA considera que el JNE ha actuado 'apegado a la normativa vigente'|url=https://elcomercio.pe/politica/elecciones/mision-de-observacion-de-la-oea-considera-que-el-jne-ha-actuado-apegado-a-la-normativa-vigente-elecciones-generales-del-peru-2021-nndc-noticia/?ref=ecr|access-date=24 June 2021|website=El Comercio|language=es}}</ref> Former candidate [[George Forsyth (footballer)|George Forsyth]] attributed it as part of the preparation of a "coup d'etat" and that Arce himself was "attacking democracy."<ref>{{cite web|date=24 June 2021|title=George Forsyth cuestiona declinación de Luis Arce a participar en el Pleno del JNE|url=https://peru21.pe/politica/george-forsyth-cuestiona-declinacion-de-luis-arce-a-participar-en-el-pleno-del-jne-nndc-noticia/|url-status=live|access-date=24 June 2021|website=Peru21|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210624184350/https://peru21.pe/politica/george-forsyth-cuestiona-declinacion-de-luis-arce-a-participar-en-el-pleno-del-jne-nndc-noticia/ |archive-date=24 June 2021 }}</ref>

==== International ====
Leftist leaders in Latin America congratulated Castillo shortly after preliminary results were tallied.<ref>{{Cite news|date=11 June 2021|title=Peru's Castillo on Verge of Being Named President After Last-Minute Vote Wrangling|website=[[U.S. News & World Report]]|agency=[[Reuters]]|url=https://www.usnews.com/news/world/articles/2021-06-11/perus-socialist-party-chief-cites-victory-as-vote-count-nears-end|access-date=23 June 2021|archive-date=21 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210621162022/https://www.usnews.com/news/world/articles/2021-06-11/perus-socialist-party-chief-cites-victory-as-vote-count-nears-end|url-status=live}}</ref> [[President of Argentina]] [[Alberto Fernández]] tweeted that he had spoken to the "President-elect" Castillo and that he wished to cooperate with him.<ref name=":36">{{cite news|date=10 June 2021|title='People Have Awakened': Peru's Castillo Closes in on Election Win|website=[[U.S. News & World Report]]|agency=[[Reuters]]|url=https://www.usnews.com/news/world/articles/2021-06-10/victory-in-sight-for-perus-castillo-with-70-000-vote-margin-as-fraud-claims-muddy-water|access-date=23 June 2021|archive-date=24 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210624203208/https://www.usnews.com/news/world/articles/2021-06-10/victory-in-sight-for-perus-castillo-with-70-000-vote-margin-as-fraud-claims-muddy-water|url-status=live}}</ref> [[President of Bolivia]] [[Luis Arce]] tweeted that "Bolivia joins the celebration of the Peruvian people", calling Castillo his "brother", and stating that the two would "continue the struggle for a tomorrow with justice and equality for the people."<ref>{{cite web|title=Arce felicita a Castillo y a Perú y dice que la 'Patria Grande' suma fuerzas|url=https://www.swissinfo.ch/spa/per%C3%BA-elecciones_arce-felicita-a-castillo-y-a-per%C3%BA-y-dice-que-la--patria-grande--suma-fuerzas/46696162|access-date=24 June 2021|website=SwissInfo|date=10 June 2021 |agency=EFE|language=es|archive-date=11 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210611021724/https://www.swissinfo.ch/spa/per%C3%BA-elecciones_arce-felicita-a-castillo-y-a-per%C3%BA-y-dice-que-la--patria-grande--suma-fuerzas/46696162|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Evo Morales]] and [[Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva]], former presidents of Bolivia and Brazil, respectively, also congratulated Castillo.<ref name=":36"/>

[[Ned Price]], [[Spokesperson for the United States Department of State]], described the elections as "a model of democracy", agreeing that it was necessary to give time to the electoral authorities to publish the results according to Peruvian law,<ref>{{cite web|date=22 June 2021|title=Estados Unidos da la espalda a Keiko Fujimori y califica las elecciones de Perú de 'justas' y 'modélicas'|url=https://elpais.com/internacional/2021-06-23/estados-unidos-da-la-espalda-a-fujimori-y-califica-las-elecciones-de-peru-de-justas-y-modelicas.html|url-status=live|access-date=23 June 2021|website=[[El País]]|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210623021329/https://elpais.com/internacional/2021-06-23/estados-unidos-da-la-espalda-a-fujimori-y-califica-las-elecciones-de-peru-de-justas-y-modelicas.html |archive-date=23 June 2021 }}</ref> while also stating: "We congratulate the Peruvian authorities for safely administering another round of free, fair, accessible and peaceful elections, even amid the significant challenges of the COVID-19 pandemic."<ref>{{cite news|date=22 June 2021|title=Washington calls Peru election 'fair' despite Fujimori claims of voter fraud|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/washington-calls-peru-election-fair-despite-fujimori-claims-voter-fraud-2021-06-22/|access-date=23 June 2021|website=[[Reuters]]|archive-date=23 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210623000116/https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/washington-calls-peru-election-fair-despite-fujimori-claims-voter-fraud-2021-06-22/|url-status=live}}</ref> The [[European Union]] described the election as "free and democratic."<ref name=":4"/>

[[Andrés Pastrana Arango]], former [[President of Colombia]] and member of the international forum IDEA (Spanish: ''Iniciativa Democrática de España y las Américas''), declared that there are "serious indications that Venezuela has its hands in the Peruvian electoral system", suggesting an international audit of the electoral results.<ref>{{cite web|date=17 June 2021|title=Andrés Pastrana reafirmó que 'hay serios indicios de que Venezuela tiene sus manos metidas en el sistema electoral peruano'|url=https://www.expreso.com.pe/elecciones-2021/andres-pastrana-reafirmo-que-hay-serios-indicios-de-que-venezuela-tiene-sus-manos-metidas-en-el-sistema-electoral-peruano/|access-date=23 June 2021|website=Diario Expreso|language=es}}</ref> The claim was rejected by the Peruvian National Office of Electoral Processes, which assured that the vote count was done transparently.<ref>{{cite web|date=18 June 2021|title=ONPE de Perú a Andrés Pastrana: 'no compartas fake news'|url=https://www.dw.com/es/onpe-de-per%C3%BA-a-andr%C3%A9s-pastrana-no-compartas-fake-news/a-57946019|url-status=live|access-date=23 June 2021|website=[[Deutsche Welle]]|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210618010134/https://www.dw.com/es/onpe-de-per%C3%BA-a-andr%C3%A9s-pastrana-no-compartas-fake-news/a-57946019 |archive-date=18 June 2021 }}</ref> Peruvian Nobel laureate residing in Spain [[Mario Vargas Llosa]] expressed his support for electoral authorities to carefully review the contested acts, saying that what is important is to have a president "that the majority of Peruvian voters has chosen and not a fraudulent president."<ref>{{cite web|date=20 June 2021|title='No le quiten el cuerpo a la jeringa'|url=https://larepublica.pe/domingo/2021/06/20/no-le-quiten-el-cuerpo-a-la-jeringa/?ref=lre|url-status=live|accessdate=23 June 2021|website=[[La República (Peru)|La República]]|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210624204859/https://larepublica.pe/domingo/2021/06/20/no-le-quiten-el-cuerpo-a-la-jeringa/?ref=lre |archive-date=24 June 2021 }}</ref> Colombian president [[Iván Duque Márquez|Iván Duque]] and Ecuadorian president [[Guillermo Lasso]] congratulated Castillo in July for his proclamation.<ref>{{cite web|date=19 July 2021|title=Presidentes de Colombia, Ecuador y Bolivia felicitan a Pedro Castillo por proclamación|url=https://andina.pe/agencia/noticia-presidentes-colombia-ecuador-y-bolivia-felicitan-a-pedro-castillo-proclamacion-853959.aspx|url-status=live|access-date=20 July 2021|website=Andina|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210720034030/https://andina.pe/agencia/noticia-presidentes-colombia-ecuador-y-bolivia-felicitan-a-pedro-castillo-proclamacion-853959.aspx |archive-date=20 July 2021 }}</ref>

=== Public opinion ===
In late June, an IEP poll showed that thirty-one percent of participants believed in Fujimori's claims of fraud.<ref name=":37" /> A statistical analysis of the company Ipsos Peru on the results published by the National Office of Electoral Processes did not find evidence of an atypical distribution of votes to any candidate, neither in certain geographical areas nor for a particular candidate.<ref>{{cite news|date=2021-06-19|title=Ipsos Perú: No se encuentra evidencia de una concentración atípica de casos a favor de un candidato en particular|url=https://elcomercio.pe/politica/elecciones/elecciones-2021-ipsos-peru-no-se-encuentra-evidencia-de-una-concentracion-atipica-de-casos-ni-en-determinadas-zonas-geograficas-ni-para-un-candidato-en-particular-fuerza-popular-peru-libre-nndc-noticia/|url-status=live|access-date=2021-06-23|website=[[El Comercio (Peru)|El Comercio]]|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210619222835/https://elcomercio.pe/politica/elecciones/elecciones-2021-ipsos-peru-no-se-encuentra-evidencia-de-una-concentracion-atipica-de-casos-ni-en-determinadas-zonas-geograficas-ni-para-un-candidato-en-particular-fuerza-popular-peru-libre-nndc-noticia/ |archive-date=19 June 2021 }}</ref> In a survey carried out by Datum Internacional, 65% of respondents (both Pedro Castillo and Keiko Fujimori voters) believed that there were "signs" of fraud in the elections.<ref>{{cite web|date=2021-06-23|title=El 65% de los peruanos cree que hay "indicios" de fraude, según encuesta|url=https://www.vanguardia.com/mundo/el-65-de-los-peruanos-cree-que-hay-indicios-de-fraude-segun-encuesta-YI3912405|url-status=live|access-date=2021-06-22|website=Vanguardia|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210622160616/https://www.vanguardia.com/mundo/el-65-de-los-peruanos-cree-que-hay-indicios-de-fraude-segun-encuesta-YI3912405 |archive-date=22 June 2021 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=2021-06-23|title=Datum: 65% de peruanos percibe que hay indicios de fraude en la segunda vuelta|url=https://gestion.pe/peru/politica/datum-65-de-los-peruanos-percibe-que-hay-indicios-de-fraude-en-segunda-vuelta-nndc-noticia/|url-status=live|access-date=2021-06-20|website=Gestión|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210621050840/https://gestion.pe/peru/politica/datum-65-de-los-peruanos-percibe-que-hay-indicios-de-fraude-en-segunda-vuelta-nndc-noticia/ |archive-date=21 June 2021 }}</ref> A survey by the Institute of Peruvian Studies showed that 66% of participants considered that Castillo had won the election.<ref>{{cite web|date=2021-06-22|title=Encuesta IEP: 66% de peruanos considera a Pedro Castillo como el ganador de las elecciones|url=https://larepublica.pe/elecciones/2021/06/22/pedro-castillo-el-66-de-los-peruanos-lo-considera-el-ganador-de-las-elecciones-2021-segun-iep-pltc/|url-status=live|access-date=2021-06-23|website=[[La República (Peru)|La República]]|language=es|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210622143751/https://larepublica.pe/elecciones/2021/06/22/pedro-castillo-el-66-de-los-peruanos-lo-considera-el-ganador-de-las-elecciones-2021-segun-iep-pltc/ |archive-date=22 June 2021 }}</ref>

